aising money he says  this is just so important that it's kind  of a fork in the road that will have an  impact for decades adding his voice to  the demands is former Republican  governor of Massachusetts William weld  William weld is you might have heard  mounting a primary challenge  Donald Trump and William weld is not  only of the mind that Trump should be  impeached he is a Republican who is  straight up calling for the resignation  of Donald Trump at this point in time  and where I disagree with William weld  is that in an op-ed that he wrote weld  said the country would be quote better  served with a president like Mike Pence  I don't think that that's true Pence is  a disgusting partisan ideologue with  extremist religious views and in  different ways than Trump is a disaster  for the country Pence would be a  disaster for the country but where I  agree with William weld is that we do  need to put aside the kind of  calculation about who would replace  Trump if Trump resigned or if Trump were  impeached this is a longtime Republican  who was a governor a governor who says  this can't go on this this has to stop  and meanwhile the administration that  told us it would be the most transparent  administration remember Trump told us  that it would be Trump press secretary  Sarah Huckabee Sanders has insisted that  it is the most transparent  administration they have not had a press  briefing in a record it's either 44 or  45 days at this point in time I don't  even know the exact number of days and  during that 40-plus day period during  which there has been no press briefing  we learned from the content of the  Muller report that Sarah Huckabee  Sanders admits to straight-up having  lied during press briefings and so there  are more and more calls for her to quit  or to resign or for someone to fire her  I guess it would be Donald Trump  basically for her to go away one way or  the other and let's talk about the Sarah  Huckabee Sanders thing a little bit I  und